# Cloudflare Pages response headers for possessio.io (build output dir = public).
# ACTIVE below: safe, non-breaking headers + a REPORT-ONLY CSP (monitors, never
# blocks — see W-2 block). ENFORCING CSP and the frame policy stay COMMENTED on
# purpose: an enforcing CSP can break the site if wrong and cannot be verified
# from CI, so it flips on only after an on-device pass (wallet connect, cdnjs
# ethers, Google Fonts, DexScreener/GeckoTerminal feeds + token images, the
# miniapp SDK) shows the Report-Only console clean. Codebyte Law: do not ENFORCE
# what you cannot verify — monitoring first is the verification step.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()

# --- Content-Security-Policy (W-2) ---
# SHIPPED IN REPORT-ONLY MODE below: the browser evaluates the policy and logs
# any violation to the console (visible in MIB DEBUG on device) but BLOCKS
# NOTHING. That is deliberate and Codebyte-Law-clean: a CSP cannot be verified
# from CI and a wrong one breaks wallet-connect, so we monitor first, enforce
# after the on-device report comes back empty. Flip Report-Only -> enforcing by
# uncommenting the second line (and only then).
#
# Allowlist is GROUNDED in what the code actually loads (grep of public/, 2026-08-26):
#   script  : self + inline (console is inline-heavy) + cdnjs (ethers 6.13.4)
#             + esm.sh (the pinned @farcaster/miniapp-sdk@0.3.0 dynamic import)
#   style   : self + inline + fonts.googleapis.com
#   font    : fonts.gstatic.com
#   connect : self + api.dexscreener.com + api.geckoterminal.com (coin feeds)
#             + the Base READ RPCs hit directly by the JsonRpcProvider ladder
#               (mainnet.base.org, base-rpc.publicnode.com, 1rpc.io) + eth.llamarpc.com
#               (L1 read) + esm.sh (module fetch). NOTE: the earlier draft omitted
#               these RPCs on the assumption all wallet RPC is via the injected
#               provider — true for WRITES, but the read path is a page-origin fetch,
#               so enforcing without them would break every on-chain read.
#   img     : self + data: + https: (DexScreener/GeckoTerminal token logos, canvas-drawn)
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://esm.sh; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.dexscreener.com https://api.geckoterminal.com https://mainnet.base.org https://base-rpc.publicnode.com https://1rpc.io https://eth.llamarpc.com https://esm.sh; img-src 'self' data: https:; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
# ENFORCE (uncomment ONLY after a device pass shows the Report-Only console clean):
# Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://esm.sh; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.dexscreener.com https://api.geckoterminal.com https://mainnet.base.org https://base-rpc.publicnode.com https://1rpc.io https://eth.llamarpc.com https://esm.sh; img-src 'self' data: https:; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'

# --- Framing policy (DECISION for the Architect) ---
# Standalone security wants DENY. But if the console is ever embedded as a
# Base App / Farcaster mini-app (webview/iframe), DENY blocks it. Left OFF so
# a future embed is not silently broken. Pick one when that path is decided:
#   X-Frame-Options: DENY
#   (or) Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://<embedder-origins>
